# build output
target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta

# test artefacts and captures: large, and they contain MAC addresses,
# network names and hostnames from the machines they were taken on
*.bin
*.pcap
*.sums
*.parts
*.csv
*.log
session-*/
rate-test-*/
data-rate-*/

# never
*.pem
*.key
.env

# Built packages: these belong on a release page, not in the history.
packaging/build/

# ...but the transfer measurements ARE kept. bench/transfer-watch.py records
# aggregate counters only: bytes, packets, retries, signal averaged across
# clients, temperature, watts. No MAC address, no hostname, no address, no
# payload. That is the whole point of it, and the data is worthless for
# improving anything if it lives only on one laptop.
!bench/results/*.csv
# The packet captures stay out. Those really do carry MACs and addresses.
bench/results/capture-*/
